{#
 # A boolean field, submitted with the form around it.
 #
 # A checkbox and not a switch: a switch says the choice takes effect as it is flipped, and neither
 # "se souvenir de moi" nor "appareil de confiance" does anything until the form is sent. It is also
 # what every other boolean in the app already looks like — `bootstrap_5_layout` renders `CheckboxType`
 # through these same classes — so a hand-written form matches the themed ones.
 #
 # `label` is a prop rather than the body because a checkbox is nothing without its label, and the
 # `for`/`id` pairing is the whole point — leaving it to the call site is leaving it to be forgotten.
 #
 # There is no size prop: the box these two pages wanted — big enough not to read as an afterthought
 # between two 48px fields, big enough to aim at with a thumb — is now what every checkbox in the app
 # is, from `$form-check-input-width` in `_custom.scss`.
 #}
{% props id, label %}

<div class="form-check">
    <input type="checkbox" class="form-check-input" id="{{ id }}"{{ attributes }}>
    <label class="form-check-label" for="{{ id }}">{{ label }}</label>
</div>
